# Storefront component structure

When creating or editing storefront UI, follow `.cursor/skills/storefront-component-structure/SKILL.md`.

- Features live in `features/<name>/` with a public `index.ts`. Folders still under `components/<name>/` are unmigrated; `components/ui/` stays flat.
- Each styled component has a colocated `name.module.css` imported as `styles`, with camelCase classes.
- Values come from `styles/tokens.css`; breakpoints use `@media (--phone)`, `(--tablet)`, `(--desktop)`, `(--wide)` and friends.
- Classes owned by other components or shared helpers (`.section`, `.button`) are wrapped in `:global()`.
- Feature-wide custom properties are shared with `composes` from a feature module.
- Nest children inside the parent folder. A component with no children is a single file. Never use `index.tsx` for a component.
- Types used only by a feature live in `type/`, constants in `const/`, hooks in the owning parent's `hooks/`.
- `app/` imports feature barrels (`@/features/cart`), not grandchildren. Inside a feature, use relative imports.
